# Temporal.PlainDateTime, in the ISO 8601 calendar (docs/temporal.md).
# Every expected value was generated by temporal-polyfill 1.0.5 (the
# vendored tests/vendor/temporal-polyfill, which diff-node runs as Temporal)
# and is the same in @js-temporal/polyfill 0.5.1. A RangeError or a
# TypeError there is a fault here. A case named "deliberate" faults where
# JavaScript gives a value: a conversion of a string, an array or an
# object, identity, locale data, a calendar other than ISO 8601's, or what
# staticjs does not build yet. temporal_test sweeps the strings, round's
# units, increments and modes, toString's digits, the limits and the
# overflow options further (diff-node compares its lines too).

# --- The constructor

=== new Temporal.PlainDateTime
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 13, 5, 9, 1, 2, 3)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T13:05:09.001002003")

=== the time defaults to midnight, and undefined is 0
[new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31), new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 1, undefined, 3)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T00:00:00"),Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T01:00:03")]

=== the writer writes Temporal.PlainDateTime.from of the ISO string
[new Temporal.PlainDateTime(0, 1, 1), new Temporal.PlainDateTime(10000, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 400), new Temporal.PlainDateTime(-1, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59, 999, 999, 999)]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("0000-01-01T00:00:00"),Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("+010000-01-01T01:02:03.4"),Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("-000001-12-31T23:59:59.999999999")]

=== the calendar iso8601, in any case of its letters
[new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, "iso8601"), new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, "ISO8601")]
--- value
[Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T00:00:00"),Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T00:00:00")]

=== another calendar, deliberate
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, "gregory")
--- fault only the ISO 8601 calendar

=== the fields are cut toward zero, and booleans and null convert
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024.9, 1.5, 31.9, true, null, 2.5)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2024-01-31T01:00:02")

=== a missing day
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1)
--- fault NaN, infinite or undefined

=== hour 24
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 24)
--- fault outside its range

=== a negative nanosecond
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, -1)
--- fault outside its range

=== February 30th
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 2, 30, 12)
--- fault day outside its month

=== month 13
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 13, 1)
--- fault month outside 1 to 12

=== a string field, deliberate
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31, "12")
--- fault converts only numbers

=== the least date and time: a nanosecond after -271821-04-19T00:00
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(-271821, 4, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("-271821-04-19T00:00:00.000000001")

=== -271821-04-19T00:00 itself
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(-271821, 4, 19)
--- fault outside Temporal's limits

=== the greatest date and time
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(275760, 9, 13, 23, 59, 59, 999, 999, 999)
--- value
Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("+275760-09-13T23:59:59.999999999")

=== the day after the greatest
new Temporal.PlainDateTime(275760, 9, 14)
--- fault outside Temporal's limits

=== a constructor called without new
Temporal.PlainDateTime(2024, 1, 31)
--- error unsupported used only as Math.name

